{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1410757-humble-solar-craftsman-a-solar-craft-revision-peach","id":1410757,"title":"Humble Solar Craftsman: A Solar Craft Revision [PEACH]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-27T13:45:11-07:00","id":1410757,"title":"Humble Solar Craftsman: A Solar Craft Revision [PEACH]","content":"Yes, this is yet another thread about the Craft system. I've done two attempts at deep rewrites of the Craft system (one of which you can find in my signature /shameless plug), but I know there's a lot of people who don't think the underlying system is broken, just that the Solar Craft Charms allow a player to ramp up to producing legendary wonders far too quickly while also having redundant Charms scattered all over the place. For those folks, I've created this:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YFIL7pRO3pgfX783L7E4h_kdxC1QNvINul0aglU0zbg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Humble Solar Craftsman: Revised Solar Craft Charms</a><br /> <br /> Most of the changes are to Charm minimums and prerequisites, so you can review the largest portion of this by just scanning the diagrams. Please, let me know what you think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T14:28:36-07:00","id":1410764,"title":"","content":"None of the changes immediately stand out as a problem (though it's a bit hard to follow changes, new additions, and so on visually for me).<br /> <br /> I feel like it doesn't address some of the low level frustrations with the RAW Craft Trees: having to constantly buy Charms (whether new ones, or repurchases) rather than using the automatic upgrade options. Why not collapse Tireless Workhorse Method, Dragon-Soul Emergence, and God-Forge Within into one Charm that automatically upgrades at Essence 3 and 4? Having to buy 11 Charms (the second two each have Essence Repurchases instead of automatically granting slots per Essence like TWM) just to have a bunch of permanent slots is the kind of bloat nobody likes, and makes people feel like Solar Craft is fighting the Crafting rules instead of making them more fun to use.<br /> <br /> I really wish Bright-Forging Prana did something after you bought all the other Charms, even as a side Charm you never have to buy, the fact that it eventually becomes worthless is still a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T16:08:41-07:00","id":1410777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1410757-humble-solar-craftsman-a-solar-craft-revision-peach?p=1410764#post1410764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of the changes immediately stand out as a problem (though it's a bit hard to follow changes, new additions, and so on visually for me).</div> </div> </div> </div>Biggest structural changes:<ul><li>Slot-granting charms have the slot-discounting Charms as prerequisites, not the other way around, and are now off the main spine of the Efficiency tree.</li> <li>Vice-Miracle Technique is now only 4 Charms deep in the Efficiency tree instead of 6 and Wonder Forging Genius is only 8 Charms deep instead of 12.</li> <li>All of the Charms for gaining Craft points that were used as speed bumps in the Efficiency tree are now part of the Inspiration tree.</li> <li>The Reforging tree is a little more squat, with a few Charms available sooner, but the more potent ones still at their same depth. Celestial Reforging Technique and Design Beyond Limit are reversed in order.</li> <li>I pushed Holistic Miracle Understanding deeper in the Power tree. Instead of being 7 Charms deep it is now 10 Charms deep. Less able to be nabbed with Bright Forging Prana out of the starting gate.</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why not collapse Tireless Workhorse Method, Dragon-Soul Emergence, and God-Forge Within into one Charm that automatically upgrades at Essence 3 and 4? Having to buy 11 Charms (the second two each have Essence Repurchases instead of automatically granting slots per Essence like TWM) just to have a bunch of permanent slots is the kind of bloat nobody likes, and makes people feel like Solar Craft is fighting the Crafting rules instead of making them more fun to use. </div> </div> </div>I can see why they did it that way. The base system treats project slots as a valuable commodity and they aren't equivalent in resource cost. A major slot is worth 5 silver points, a superior slot is worth up to 5 gold points and 25 silver points, and a legendary slot is worth 5 white points. Add on top of that the system doesn't explicitly let you use a higher slot for a lower project and keeping them separate makes sense. The major problem with those were they were located along the main spine of the Efficiency tree, forcing people to pick them up along with Summit-Piercing Touch along the way to Vice-Miracle Technique and Dual Magnus Prana, so no one ever really valued slots as a Solar because they always had the one slot they needed. Tthe base system creating incentives to have only one superior project at a time exacerbated the problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I really wish Bright-Forging Prana did something after you bought all the other Charms, even as a side Charm you never have to buy, the fact that it eventually becomes worthless is still a problem. </div> </div> </div>Did you consider homebrew Charms and eventual post-Essence 5 Charms? There's hypothetically infinite Charms in each Ability. I also figure that people with Bright Forging Prana will find a handful of Charms they don't normally need and just use Bright Forging Prana to pull them out when necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}